+status: production
+domain: neuropathology
+framework_name: 'AD co-pathology neuropathologic staging recommended by NIA-AA 2012: LATE-NC (limbic-predominant
+  age-related TDP-43 encephalopathy) stage and Lewy-related alpha-synuclein category. Co-pathology is
+  present in a majority of autopsy-confirmed AD and modifies the cognitive trajectory.'
+transcribed_by: Salokhiddinov M, MD PhD (KIUT, Uzbekistan), 2026-05-29. LATE-NC stage 0-3 verbatim from
+  Nelson PT et al. Brain 2019;142(6):1503-1527 (DOI 10.1093/brain/awz099). Lewy alpha-synuclein categories
+  (modified McKeith) per NIA-AA 2012 (Hyman/Montine 2012) and McKeith IG et al. Neurology 2017 DLB consortium.
+clinical_source_authority: |-
+  This pack encodes the two highest-frequency AD co-pathologies the NIA-AA 2012 guideline recommends assessing at autopsy. NeuroTCS audits neuropathologist-assigned values against the defined consensus ranges; it does not perform the assessment.
+
+  Measurements:
+   - late_nc_stage: 0-3 (Nelson PT et al. Brain 2019 LATE consensus). 0=none, 1=amygdala, 2=+hippocampus/entorhinal, 3=+neocortex.
+   - lewy_alpha_synuclein_category: none / brainstem_predominant / limbic_transitional / neocortical / amygdala_predominant (modified McKeith categories per NIA-AA 2012; McKeith 2017 DLB consortium).
+
+  Bounds are defined consensus scale ranges/categories; values outside them are coding/data errors. Braak alpha-synuclein 0-VI staging and autopsy cerebrovascular grades are deferred to a future pack pending in-session citation verification (research discipline, not omission).
+anchor_citation:
+  citation_text: 'Nelson PT, Dickson DW, Trojanowski JQ, et al. Limbic-predominant age-related TDP-43
+    encephalopathy (LATE): consensus working group report. Brain 2019;142(6):1503-1527 (DOI 10.1093/brain/awz099).
